{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01946",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.15,
      "end_seconds": 4.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.15,
      "end_seconds": 10.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "So, of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.56,
      "end_seconds": 17.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Mm, doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.61,
      "end_seconds": 21.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "I'm here because of vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.87,
      "end_seconds": 25.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.9,
      "end_seconds": 27.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.65,
      "end_seconds": 32.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Has there been the worst headache of your life too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.45,
      "end_seconds": 52.42,
      "duration_seconds": 18.97,
      "text": "Yes, for six months. With worst headache of my life, maybe a six out of ten on a bad day. Honestly, on and off. I've had a stiff neck too, for about two weeks. With stiff neck, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.93,
      "end_seconds": 66.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Right, can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.52,
      "end_seconds": 76.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening for the blood thinning. I take lamotrigine, 100 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.28,
      "end_seconds": 88.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.26,
      "end_seconds": 95.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Oh, yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.5,
      "end_seconds": 115.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.62,
      "end_seconds": 123.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for two years now. I've had epilepsy, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.21,
      "end_seconds": 135.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Alright, an irregular heartbeat, that matches what I have here. How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.73,
      "end_seconds": 138.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.76,
      "end_seconds": 141.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.53,
      "end_seconds": 146.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.39,
      "end_seconds": 151.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "So, have you noticed weakness, fever or head injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.46,
      "end_seconds": 156.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.33,
      "end_seconds": 161.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.69,
      "end_seconds": 162.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.12,
      "end_seconds": 167.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.26,
      "end_seconds": 171.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.2,
      "end_seconds": 177.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.25,
      "end_seconds": 186.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.87,
      "end_seconds": 207.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 89, SpO2 99 percent on room air. And temperature 36.4, blood pressure 156 over 99."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.97,
      "end_seconds": 210.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.7,
      "end_seconds": 213.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.49,
      "end_seconds": 219.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.12,
      "end_seconds": 224.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.89,
      "end_seconds": 237.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Your neck is stiff and you are very sensitive to light."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.15,
      "end_seconds": 258.61,
      "duration_seconds": 18.46,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Putting it all together, the most likely explanation is a possible bleed around the brain. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Another possibility is a migraine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.11,
      "end_seconds": 263.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Hmm, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.1,
      "end_seconds": 288.65,
      "duration_seconds": 24.55,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a possible bleed around the brain, and we'll know more once the a lumbar puncture is back. I'm going to order a lumbar puncture, for thunderclap headache. This needs an emergency scan, an ambulance is on its way. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.46,
      "end_seconds": 293.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Yes, I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.24,
      "end_seconds": 298.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.02,
      "end_seconds": 302.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.21,
      "end_seconds": 305.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.74,
      "end_seconds": 308.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}